# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
#   https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/1078
# Symptom: some fields in a line are tab-separated while others are
#   space-separated; this inconsistency arises when BED files are
#   processed by awk scripts that use printf with mixed "%s\t" and "%s "
#   format strings, or when copy-paste from documentation introduces spaces.
#   Tools that split strictly on tabs will split the space-separated
#   fields incorrectly; tools that split on any whitespace may produce
#   the correct field count by accident.
chr1	100	200 feature001	0	+
chr1	300	400	feature002 0	-
